        "annotations": [
          {
            "id": "an1",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -12.8,
            "text": "LM7805 under load"
          },
          {
            "id": "an2",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -11,
            "text": "The same 9 V to 5 V supply with an electronic load on its output, drawing",
            "color": "#808080"
          },
          {
            "id": "an3",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -9.2,
            "text": "300 mA. The regulator burns the difference — (9 V − 5 V) × 0.3 A = 1.2 W — and",
            "color": "#808080"
          },
          {
            "id": "an4",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -7.4,
            "text": "past 1 W in free air it runs hot (a warning, under Spice Lite). Raise the load",
            "color": "#808080"
          },
          {
            "id": "an5",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -5.6,
            "text": "past 2 W and its thermal shutdown trips: the output goes, and comes back as it",
            "color": "#808080"
          },
          {
            "id": "an6",
            "kind": "label",
            "x": 0,
            "y": -3.8,
            "text": "cools. Set the load's current in its Properties; it reads out V, A and W.",
            "color": "#808080"
          }
        ],
